OneTimeUseIdPolicy::initializeWithMultiplexer
├── given initData is neither 64 nor 84 bytes
│   └── it should revert with InvalidInitDataLength
├── given initData carries an id but no deadline
│   └── it should revert with InvalidInitDataLength
├── given initData carries a truncated wrapped-native address
│   └── it should revert with InvalidInitDataLength
├── given initData carries a wrapped-native address
│   └── it should let checkAction pass a deposit() on it behind a consumeFor
├── given the id is zero
│   └── it should revert with InvalidId
├── given a different multiplexer never installed this configId
│   └── it should see no configuration (checkAction fails closed)
├── given the id was already burned
│   └── when re-initializing with the same id
│       └── it should not restore the spend
├── given the id was already burned
│   └── when re-initializing with a fresh id
│       └── it should settle again
├── given the deadline has already passed
│   └── it should revert with DeadlineInPast
├── given the deadline is the current timestamp
│   └── it should be accepted, matching the inclusive read rule
└── given the deadline is zero
    └── it should never expire
